WEBVTT

00:02.002 --> 00:03.671
Imperial Calendar Year 955.

00:03.671 --> 00:06.507
The battleships
of the Star Forces...

00:06.507 --> 00:09.510
...had countered the advances
of the Triple Alliance...

00:09.510 --> 00:13.480
...which consisted of
the United Mankind...

00:13.480 --> 00:13.881
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

00:13.881 --> 00:16.750
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...the Republic of Greater Alcont...

00:16.750 --> 00:17.985
Imperial Capital Lakfakalle
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

00:17.985 --> 00:20.087
...and The People's Sovereign
Union of Planets.

00:20.087 --> 00:22.681
The counterattack had begun.

00:23.057 --> 00:23.757
As commander of the Third Fleet...

00:23.757 --> 00:25.659
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
As commander of the Third Fleet...

00:25.659 --> 00:30.030
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
...as well as overall
commander-in-chief...

00:30.030 --> 00:30.397
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

00:30.397 --> 00:30.831
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

00:30.831 --> 00:34.835
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
...Commander Abriel amassed
a huge fleet of 150 squadrons.

00:34.835 --> 00:35.536
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

00:35.536 --> 00:35.803
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

00:35.803 --> 00:37.204
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
Additional forces of
training ships on standby...

00:37.204 --> 00:40.574
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

00:40.574 --> 00:40.808
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

00:40.808 --> 00:44.878
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
...will provide another seventy
squadrons in the event of a battle.

00:44.878 --> 00:45.579
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
Sparing nothing...

00:45.579 --> 00:45.779
Sparing nothing...

00:45.779 --> 00:50.584
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...to reorganize the fleet
in terms of scale...

00:50.584 --> 00:55.055
...training, and top personnel,
the Star Forces have dubbed this...

00:55.055 --> 00:57.888
Operation Phantom Flame.

00:58.392 --> 01:02.488
Now, the battle will truly begin.

01:10.437 --> 01:11.739
Mines?!

01:11.739 --> 01:12.728
In a place like this?!

01:14.708 --> 01:15.970
Second Aviator!

01:17.177 --> 01:17.939
Shooting!

01:27.254 --> 01:28.346
Enemy attack?!

01:28.589 --> 01:29.283
Is it a direct hit?!

01:35.496 --> 01:39.193
Escape in the Dark

01:45.005 --> 01:49.704
Banner of the Stars

03:04.818 --> 03:06.786
Second enemy ship!
Space-time fusion!

03:10.424 --> 03:12.221
Third enemy ship!
Space-time fusion!

03:17.764 --> 03:19.933
Fourth and fifth enemy ships
approaching!

03:19.933 --> 03:21.502
Use the anti-proton cannon...

03:21.502 --> 03:23.270
...and aim it directly
at the fourth ship!

03:23.270 --> 03:24.100
Roger!

03:24.238 --> 03:24.932
Fire!

03:29.843 --> 03:31.868
The ship will respond
in five seconds!

03:32.279 --> 03:33.974
The fourth ship!
Space-time fusion!

03:38.785 --> 03:40.377
The fifth enemy ship!
Space-time fusion!

03:41.121 --> 03:42.588
Fire the rear laser cannons!

03:48.795 --> 03:50.197
Enemy assault ship...

03:50.197 --> 03:51.789
...targeting on us!

03:52.466 --> 03:55.068
Focus magnetic shield
on the right hull!

03:55.068 --> 03:56.626
Use the anti-proton cannon
to shoot them down!

03:56.837 --> 03:58.872
The ship will respond
in ten seconds!

03:58.872 --> 04:02.176
Eight... seven... six... five...

04:02.176 --> 04:03.234
- We're not going to make it!
...four...

04:07.981 --> 04:09.175
There's a message
from the Seigroil.

04:09.883 --> 04:12.519
I hope we didn't intrude, Basroil.

04:12.519 --> 04:13.687
Thank you...

04:13.687 --> 04:15.018
...Captain Ragash.

04:15.522 --> 04:16.523
No problem.

04:16.523 --> 04:18.358
You weren't doing too badly
for a newcomer.

04:18.358 --> 04:19.459
Uh-oh...

04:19.459 --> 04:22.724
Watch out behind you.
Direction 172 degrees 24 minutes.

04:23.797 --> 04:25.355
Shoot it down with
the laser cannon!

04:28.635 --> 04:29.932
In actual fact...

04:30.137 --> 04:32.139
Phantom Flame Flagship
Third Fleet, Patrol Ship Sankau
...the First Fleet of Admiral Spoor...

04:32.139 --> 04:35.042
Phantom Flame Flagship
Third Fleet, Patrol Ship Sankau
...almost achieved the objectives
of Operation Phantom Flame.

04:35.042 --> 04:35.667
...almost achieved the objectives
of Operation Phantom Flame.

04:35.809 --> 04:39.479
...given the additional enemy
reconnaissance missions...

04:39.479 --> 04:42.505
...we're certain they're preparing
for a large-scale counterattack.

04:43.050 --> 04:45.819
If the First Fleet cannot make it
to the Laseese Kingdom...

04:45.819 --> 04:48.388
...the gates may be retaken
by the enemy...

04:48.388 --> 04:52.119
...cutting off our supply line
and leaving the fleet stranded.

04:52.759 --> 04:54.895
The logical choice would be
for us to...

04:54.895 --> 04:56.663
...halt the First Fleet...

04:56.663 --> 04:58.824
...and wait for the enemy to
make its first move.

05:00.167 --> 05:03.570
The gates most likely
to be targeted...

05:03.570 --> 05:06.306
...are those nearest the enemy:
Wimpel Gate...

05:06.306 --> 05:07.864
...and Miofrantia Gate.

05:08.775 --> 05:12.267
If we retreat from these gates,
leaving only reconnaissance ships...

05:13.013 --> 05:15.482
...then the only place they
can attack...

05:15.482 --> 05:18.485
...is at the gates of Aptic
and Mystel...

05:18.485 --> 05:19.918
...which lie adjacent.

05:20.654 --> 05:22.022
If we can defend these gates...

05:22.022 --> 05:24.091
...we can secure our supply line.

05:24.091 --> 05:27.628
Of course, it will take time
for the enemy fleet to rebuild.

05:27.628 --> 05:30.964
During that time, we can
easily carry out our operation.

05:30.964 --> 05:31.832
Assuming...

05:31.832 --> 05:34.901
...we're able to win the battle
that lies ahead of us, of course.

05:34.901 --> 05:38.505
That's why the chief of staff
is here today.

05:38.505 --> 05:40.941
No, that's not what I meant.

05:40.941 --> 05:41.875
Chief of Staff.

05:41.875 --> 05:43.110
Please continue.

05:43.110 --> 05:43.667
Yes, sir.

05:44.878 --> 05:48.109
Admiral Bebaus is currently
stationed in the Aptic region.

05:48.448 --> 05:51.940
Admiral Mulusufa is assembling
his fleets in the Mystel System.

05:52.319 --> 05:53.654
Our main fleet...

05:53.654 --> 05:55.422
...will head into action...

05:55.422 --> 05:57.287
...when we have enemy confirmation.

05:57.658 --> 06:00.360
Are you sure it's safe to proceed...

06:00.360 --> 06:03.227
...only after the enemy
makes its move?

06:03.430 --> 06:07.134
The question is how fast
we can read their movements.

06:07.134 --> 06:10.203
Whatever they do, we'll still
have to face them here.

06:10.203 --> 06:12.839
And we have to win,
or the whole operation...

06:12.839 --> 06:14.864
...is in danger of collapsing.

06:15.409 --> 06:17.444
In that case, we can
use reconnaissance ships...

06:17.444 --> 06:21.471
...from any of the nearby gates
as reinforcements.

06:22.049 --> 06:25.452
Our reconnaissance missions
in Wimpel and Miofrantia...

06:25.452 --> 06:28.910
...will prove to be the key
to the entire operation.

06:31.925 --> 06:32.693
And so...

06:32.693 --> 06:35.762
...our Latouche Squadron...

06:35.762 --> 06:38.598
...in the First Division of the
1058th Battalion...

06:38.598 --> 06:42.261
...was sent off on our mission
towards the Wimpel Gate.

06:42.469 --> 06:46.496
Luckily, we were the first to
discover the enemy ships.

06:46.707 --> 06:49.910
Unluckily we were the first...

06:49.910 --> 06:52.037
...to enter into battle.

07:01.154 --> 07:03.256
All mines have been
confirmed destroyed.

07:03.256 --> 07:06.157
All enemy space-time bubbles
have been eliminated.

07:08.195 --> 07:11.064
I guess they finally
ran out of things to throw at us.

07:11.064 --> 07:12.199
Damage report?

07:12.199 --> 07:15.268
A small breach in the hull
at the back, on the port side.

07:15.268 --> 07:15.936
We'll be okay.

07:15.936 --> 07:17.130
It doesn't look serious.

07:17.637 --> 07:18.572
Captain...

07:18.572 --> 07:21.132
...we've received a message
from Command HQ.

07:21.341 --> 07:22.069
Read it.

07:22.676 --> 07:25.479
The enemy's front line has been
successfully eliminated.

07:25.479 --> 07:27.071
Withdraw immediately.

07:28.014 --> 07:28.810
Withdraw?

07:29.116 --> 07:30.150
Even though we won?

07:30.150 --> 07:32.419
Our mission was to
find the enemy...

07:32.419 --> 07:34.683
...not to secure the
Wimpel Planetary System.

07:35.222 --> 07:36.590
Right.

07:36.590 --> 07:40.160
The message also says that the
main enemy fleet is advancing.

07:40.160 --> 07:40.785
Understood.

07:41.461 --> 07:42.689
Prepare to withdraw!

07:42.863 --> 07:43.530
Captain.

07:43.530 --> 07:44.929
Our space-time bubble
is starting to...

07:46.366 --> 07:47.968
They report decreased speed...

07:47.968 --> 07:50.470
...due to debris from the enemy
in their space-time bubbles.

07:50.470 --> 07:51.528
Understood.

07:52.672 --> 07:54.141
Send them this reply:

07:54.141 --> 07:58.078
"I give permission to the Basroil
and Seigroil to fall behind."

07:58.078 --> 07:59.846
"We will pray for their safe return."

07:59.846 --> 08:00.514
Roger.

08:00.514 --> 08:01.538
Sending reply now!

08:03.984 --> 08:05.110
Captain...

08:05.852 --> 08:08.855
...it's been quite a while
since you've had a break.

08:08.855 --> 08:10.624
I'll take over the watch.

08:10.624 --> 08:11.852
You should go get some rest.

08:12.959 --> 08:15.587
Yes. I think I'll do that.

08:17.764 --> 08:20.494
I want everyone else to take turns
and get some rest as well.

08:31.845 --> 08:33.278
Hey, you can't go in there!

08:34.281 --> 08:35.441
Diaho!

08:46.893 --> 08:49.453
Come on. Don't bother her, okay?

08:54.868 --> 08:56.893
Sleep well, Captain.

09:07.881 --> 09:09.249
Enemy attack?!

09:09.249 --> 09:10.517
Is it a direct hit?!

09:10.517 --> 09:12.382
Give me a status report!

09:12.586 --> 09:14.383
We're checking right now,
Captain!

09:15.088 --> 09:16.180
What happened?

09:16.656 --> 09:17.591
I don't know.

09:17.591 --> 09:18.825
Right...

09:18.825 --> 09:19.849
Jinto!

09:20.961 --> 09:21.928
Thanks a lot.

09:21.928 --> 09:24.123
That's okay.
You weren't heavy.

09:24.498 --> 09:25.226
Fool!

09:26.333 --> 09:28.768
We've got to stabilize
the pressure on the ship!

09:28.768 --> 09:30.036
I'm already working on it.

09:30.036 --> 09:32.839
But the space-time generator
is more important.

09:32.839 --> 09:33.907
I agree.

09:33.907 --> 09:34.741
Second Aviator!

09:34.741 --> 09:35.942
What about the Seigroil?

09:35.942 --> 09:38.672
Still with us. I'm trying to
get a connection now.

09:38.845 --> 09:40.547
I gather this is an emergency.

09:40.547 --> 09:43.482
I need a quick and accurate report
from you right now!

09:43.683 --> 09:45.385
We've been hit by a mine attack.

09:45.385 --> 09:46.286
A mine attack?!

09:46.286 --> 09:47.754
Go on.

09:47.754 --> 09:50.624
Although we destroyed them
with laser cannons...

09:50.624 --> 09:52.325
...the mines came in
close to us...

09:52.325 --> 09:54.594
...and several pieces of shrapnel
managed to hit the ship.

09:54.594 --> 09:56.528
The same goes for the Seigroil.

09:56.696 --> 09:57.560
Is there any damage?

09:58.598 --> 10:00.267
We're still checking it out.

10:00.267 --> 10:02.936
Pressure leaks in at least
sixteen places.

10:02.936 --> 10:05.438
And major damage to the
equipment on deck...

10:05.438 --> 10:06.962
...perhaps some moderate.

10:07.574 --> 10:09.009
Supply Officer...

10:09.009 --> 10:10.243
...work with the line wing aviator...

10:10.243 --> 10:12.212
...and assess all damage to the ship.

10:12.212 --> 10:13.144
Yes, Captain.

10:13.413 --> 10:14.981
I still can't believe how...

10:14.981 --> 10:17.609
...all those unexploded mines
would activate at the same time.

10:17.918 --> 10:18.714
At the same time?

10:19.019 --> 10:20.253
There were three aimed at us...

10:20.253 --> 10:22.022
...and four aimed at the Seigroil...

10:22.022 --> 10:25.321
...and they were all activated
within two seconds of each other.

10:26.626 --> 10:28.218
This can't be coincidence.

10:28.528 --> 10:29.119
No.

10:29.729 --> 10:30.363
Captain!

10:30.363 --> 10:32.966
We've made contact
with the Seigroil.

10:32.966 --> 10:34.701
Deca-Commander Abriel...

10:34.701 --> 10:36.803
...we have a serious situation here.

10:36.803 --> 10:38.202
How is it with you?

10:38.638 --> 10:40.907
We have suffered some
extensive damage...

10:40.907 --> 10:42.609
...but we have not fully
assessed it yet.

10:42.609 --> 10:43.337
Captain.

10:43.643 --> 10:45.702
Things don't look good here.

10:45.845 --> 10:48.837
The space-time communicator
and the radar system were hit.

10:49.649 --> 10:51.151
There's a lot of damage...

10:51.151 --> 10:52.880
...but those are the worst.

10:53.353 --> 10:56.720
We should count ourselves lucky
there were no fatalities.

10:58.091 --> 11:01.494
Sounds like you're in pretty much
the same situation as we are.

11:01.494 --> 11:02.662
Is it that bad, Seigroil?

11:02.662 --> 11:03.890
Yes. I'm afraid so.

11:04.664 --> 11:08.134
We both took a direct hit
in the same area.

11:08.134 --> 11:09.336
It's no surprise.

11:09.336 --> 11:12.396
We've become stranded
in Plane Space!

11:12.606 --> 11:17.100
And we're right in front of
the approaching enemy fleet.

11:27.253 --> 11:30.023
Repairs to stabilize the
pressure system are complete.

11:30.023 --> 11:31.047
Good work.

11:31.725 --> 11:34.250
What about the
space-time communicator?

11:34.661 --> 11:35.895
We have an idea about that.

11:35.895 --> 11:36.763
However...

11:36.763 --> 11:40.221
...we can't fix it with what we have.

11:40.433 --> 11:41.331
No...

11:42.002 --> 11:44.903
We received word from
the Seigroil a minute ago.

11:45.338 --> 11:47.741
Their space-time communicator
and radar system...

11:47.741 --> 11:49.402
...are both beyond repair.

11:49.809 --> 11:52.869
So I guess we came out of this
slightly better than they did.

11:53.546 --> 11:57.380
Does that mean that our
radar system can be fixed?

11:57.584 --> 11:59.653
It'll take six hours to do the work.

11:59.653 --> 12:00.551
Very well.

12:01.655 --> 12:04.180
I suppose all we can do now
is sit and wait.

12:05.558 --> 12:07.093
Transmission from the Seigroil!

12:07.093 --> 12:09.493
They ask that we keep the
space-time bubble stationary.

12:10.030 --> 12:10.758
Understood.

12:11.131 --> 12:12.499
In this situation...

12:12.499 --> 12:16.265
...we can't even tell what direction
the space-time bubble is headed in.

12:16.770 --> 12:18.138
And what's worse...

12:18.138 --> 12:21.041
...we won't be able to tell if there's
an enemy space-time bubble coming...

12:21.041 --> 12:22.565
...for the next six hours.

12:26.846 --> 12:29.371
Deca-Commander Abriel.
How are things going?

12:29.883 --> 12:33.080
The repairs on our radar system
have now been completed.

12:33.286 --> 12:36.551
However, I can't say things are
looking any brighter than before.

12:37.190 --> 12:39.092
The radar has deteriorated
quite badly.

12:39.092 --> 12:41.720
We can only detect objects
in close range.

12:42.962 --> 12:45.699
Right now, he can't see anything...

12:45.699 --> 12:47.360
...that's outside our range.

12:48.301 --> 12:51.271
We can't just move about
in the dark.

12:51.271 --> 12:54.107
Even if allies send a ship
to rescue us...

12:54.107 --> 12:56.268
...there's still one big hurdle
to overcome.

12:59.345 --> 13:03.406
This difficult period, which had
put an enormous strain on us...

13:03.917 --> 13:07.318
...was to last for over forty hours.

13:09.856 --> 13:12.392
Space-time bubbles
in Plane Space...

13:12.392 --> 13:15.156
...are a bit like a ball which
has fallen onto the floor.

13:15.628 --> 13:17.731
When the ball is rolling,
it travels.

13:17.731 --> 13:21.929
But when it stops rolling,
it simply spins in one position.

13:22.635 --> 13:23.970
In other words...

13:23.970 --> 13:26.072
...although we had stopped...

13:26.072 --> 13:29.337
...the space-time generator was
using up precious anti-matter fuel.

13:30.043 --> 13:31.878
In order to conserve that fuel...

13:31.878 --> 13:35.609
...we had to sacrifice some of
the ship's comforts.

13:35.815 --> 13:38.841
Eventually, there was a
change in the situation.

13:39.953 --> 13:40.715
Captain!

13:40.954 --> 13:43.115
The radar's picked up a trace
heading towards us.

13:43.456 --> 13:44.445
How big is it?

13:44.591 --> 13:46.115
About the size of a squadron.

13:46.559 --> 13:49.289
Get a message to the
Seigroil immediately.

13:50.096 --> 13:52.360
Some space-time bubbles
are approaching?!

13:52.899 --> 13:55.135
Our fuel is only going to
last about six hours.

13:55.135 --> 13:56.970
How about you, Basroil?

13:56.970 --> 13:58.904
I think we can survive
another ten hours.

13:59.506 --> 14:00.837
What's going on?

14:01.441 --> 14:03.743
We're calculating how much
longer we can run...

14:03.743 --> 14:05.540
...on the remaining fuel.

14:06.079 --> 14:06.746
Run?

14:06.746 --> 14:07.770
What for?

14:08.448 --> 14:11.785
Since our space-time
communicator is out of action...

14:11.785 --> 14:14.020
...we're not in a position to tell...

14:14.020 --> 14:16.420
...if approaching bubbles
are friendly or not.

14:17.023 --> 14:18.047
What?

14:18.758 --> 14:20.226
It's a simple calculation...

14:20.226 --> 14:22.228
...but if we combine our fuel...

14:22.228 --> 14:24.662
...we'll have sixteen hours' worth.

14:25.732 --> 14:26.630
Combine?

14:31.004 --> 14:31.738
All right.

14:31.738 --> 14:33.035
We've still got time.

14:33.740 --> 14:35.367
Don't rush it, guys!

14:36.376 --> 14:40.312
Even I don't have the courage to
play around with anti-matter fuel.

14:41.214 --> 14:43.650
Transfer their fuel
and their crew here...

14:43.650 --> 14:45.618
...and make space-time separation.

14:45.885 --> 14:47.648
Seems like a good decision.

14:49.055 --> 14:51.624
If we leave the Seigroil
and all the debris...

14:51.624 --> 14:53.960
...we can increase our speed
significantly.

14:53.960 --> 14:57.697
But isn't it risky working
inside a space-time bubble?

14:57.697 --> 15:00.066
There's still a lot of debris around.

15:00.066 --> 15:03.194
It would've been impossible,
even with a Calike.

15:03.803 --> 15:04.637
Captain.

15:04.637 --> 15:08.541
We have successfully transferred
both the fuel and the crew of...

15:08.541 --> 15:09.565
...the Seigroil onto the Basroil!

15:12.445 --> 15:13.713
So, Captain Ragash...

15:13.713 --> 15:14.781
...you heard the news.

15:14.781 --> 15:17.116
It's time for you and your
officers to come on board.

15:17.116 --> 15:18.384
I'm afraid that...

15:18.384 --> 15:20.119
...my officers and I cannot
accept your offer...

15:20.119 --> 15:21.621
...Deca-Commander Abriel.

15:21.621 --> 15:22.422
What?!

15:22.422 --> 15:23.320
Why not?!

15:23.523 --> 15:26.960
I'm sorry I didn't tell you earlier.

15:26.960 --> 15:30.919
But the damage is such that
there's no escape from the bridge.

15:31.431 --> 15:34.067
There were other areas requiring
more immediate attention.

15:34.067 --> 15:37.093
This part of the ship took
a low priority.

15:37.804 --> 15:38.938
Unfortunately...

15:38.938 --> 15:42.475
...we didn't have the time to make
an escape route for ourselves.

15:42.475 --> 15:46.312
But my honor would not allow me
to leave you stranded here...

15:46.312 --> 15:48.007
...in Plane Space with no fuel.

15:49.649 --> 15:52.719
This shouldn't be about
your personal feelings...

15:52.719 --> 15:53.743
...Your Highness.

15:54.220 --> 15:56.155
In the same way that you...

15:56.155 --> 15:58.725
...have your responsibilities
to your subjects...

15:58.725 --> 16:00.627
...an officer of the Star Forces...

16:00.627 --> 16:02.754
...has a responsibility to his crew.

16:03.196 --> 16:04.330
But Captain...

16:04.330 --> 16:07.533
I have chosen to save the lives
of most of the crew...

16:07.533 --> 16:11.264
...in the most effective way
through this decision.

16:11.804 --> 16:12.964
Am I right?

16:15.708 --> 16:17.644
Deca-Commander Abriel!

16:17.644 --> 16:20.340
I entrust my crew to your care.

16:23.249 --> 16:24.739
I promise.

16:26.920 --> 16:29.548
I end the transmission now.
Out.

16:32.992 --> 16:35.461
The gangway has been severed.

16:35.461 --> 16:37.759
The Seigroil is drifting away.

16:44.037 --> 16:44.971
Captain...

16:44.971 --> 16:46.461
...what are your orders?

16:46.806 --> 16:48.774
Begin separation.

16:49.676 --> 16:50.608
Yes, Captain.

16:53.446 --> 16:56.883
When the Basroil separated from
space-time fusion we had to...

16:56.883 --> 17:00.944
...leave the Siegroil, and those
still left on the ship, behind us.

17:02.088 --> 17:03.623
With no fuel left...

17:03.623 --> 17:05.591
...the Seigroil could not avoid...

17:05.591 --> 17:09.527
...coming into the path of the
approaching space-time bubbles.

17:10.163 --> 17:14.623
They had become a decoy, giving
their lives so we could escape.

17:15.134 --> 17:15.896
And then...

17:23.576 --> 17:26.204
The Seigroil has disappeared.

17:29.916 --> 17:31.417
The ship and those remaining...

17:31.417 --> 17:34.520
...will be transformed into
space-time particles...

17:34.520 --> 17:37.785
...and float around Plane Space
for eternity.

17:43.229 --> 17:46.130
It's getting hard to breathe in here.

17:46.399 --> 17:48.601
They're cutting back on everything...

17:48.601 --> 17:50.436
...probably even the air supply.

17:50.436 --> 17:54.440
And how much fuel are we
going to save by doing that?!

17:54.440 --> 17:55.441
Five minutes?

17:55.441 --> 17:56.342
Ten minutes?!

17:56.342 --> 17:57.832
How the hell should I know?

17:58.411 --> 17:59.712
Damn!

17:59.712 --> 18:02.849
Why don't we just surrender to
those bubbles chasing us?

18:02.849 --> 18:05.952
A prisoner-of-war camp?
Or being stuck in Plane Space?

18:05.952 --> 18:07.544
I wonder which is better.

18:08.921 --> 18:09.856
No.

18:09.856 --> 18:10.788
I can't permit it.

18:11.424 --> 18:14.460
I figured that would
be your response.

18:14.460 --> 18:15.862
More than half the crew...

18:15.862 --> 18:18.031
...say they want to surrender.

18:18.031 --> 18:20.366
Even if those space-time
bubbles are the enemy...

18:20.366 --> 18:22.869
...if we run out of fuel
in the meantime...

18:22.869 --> 18:24.598
It hasn't happened yet.

18:24.937 --> 18:27.303
We'll retreat until we're left
with no choice.

18:29.675 --> 18:31.677
I think everybody's
reached their limit.

18:31.677 --> 18:34.737
Their nerves will run out
before the fuel does.

18:36.115 --> 18:37.483
It's my duty...

18:37.483 --> 18:39.951
...to bring everyone back alive.

18:42.488 --> 18:44.991
Another group of space-time
bubbles ahead of us.

18:44.991 --> 18:47.026
About the size of one squadron.

18:47.026 --> 18:48.361
From the front?!

18:48.361 --> 18:49.128
Captain...

18:49.128 --> 18:50.493
...what should we do?

18:51.464 --> 18:52.396
Captain?

19:11.050 --> 19:14.220
The space-time bubbles
ahead of us are ours.

19:14.220 --> 19:15.778
Continue to advance.

19:16.255 --> 19:17.517
Y-yes, Captain!

19:20.626 --> 19:21.427
Captain!

19:21.427 --> 19:25.164
A smaller space-time bubble
has been released ahead!

19:25.164 --> 19:26.632
I think it's a mine!

19:26.632 --> 19:27.800
A mine?!

19:27.800 --> 19:28.468
Damn.

19:28.468 --> 19:30.103
We can't dodge it at this distance.

19:30.103 --> 19:33.272
We don't have enough power
left to fire the laser cannon!

19:33.272 --> 19:34.173
I don't care.

19:34.173 --> 19:36.342
Maintain course and speed.

19:36.342 --> 19:38.177
Ten seconds until
space-time fusion!

19:38.177 --> 19:42.081
Eight... seven... six... five...

19:42.081 --> 19:45.051
...four... three... two...

19:45.051 --> 19:45.985
...one.

19:45.985 --> 19:47.509
Space-time fusion!

19:49.322 --> 19:51.483
The self-destruct system
is not responding!

19:52.058 --> 19:54.424
Hold on.
The mine's going right past!

19:55.027 --> 19:56.153
Misfire?!

19:56.362 --> 19:59.265
This is Star Force Defense Fleet
of the Aptic Gate.

19:59.265 --> 20:01.334
This is a message for our
fellow attack ship.

20:01.334 --> 20:04.504
Immediately enter space-time
fusion with the lead ship!

20:04.504 --> 20:05.538
I repeat.

20:05.538 --> 20:07.974
This is Star Force Defense Fleet
of the Aptic Gate.

20:07.974 --> 20:10.610
We're receiving a transmission?
But how?

20:10.610 --> 20:11.440
That's simple.

20:12.078 --> 20:14.808
The transmission isn't coming
from another space-time bubble.

20:15.948 --> 20:17.283
Then from where?

20:17.283 --> 20:21.554
What we thought was a mine
was actually a transmitter.

20:21.554 --> 20:24.457
Only one person would
think of this.

20:24.457 --> 20:27.085
It must be Unit Commander Atosuryua.

20:30.930 --> 20:31.964
Then...

20:31.964 --> 20:33.266
You heard the message!

20:33.266 --> 20:35.368
Hurry up with the
space-time fusion!

20:35.368 --> 20:36.494
Yes, Captain!

20:41.908 --> 20:43.136
Confirming the Gamroil.

20:43.910 --> 20:45.571
Making the connection now.

20:46.112 --> 20:48.548
Welcome back to the fleet,
Basroil.

20:48.548 --> 20:51.384
I'm happy to have you
with us again.

20:51.384 --> 20:52.817
Thank you, Ma'am.

20:53.352 --> 20:57.652
I'll give you the full report on the
last moments of the Siegroil later.

20:58.224 --> 21:00.126
Those space-time bubbles
chasing you...

21:00.126 --> 21:02.390
...comprise the United Mankind fleet.

21:02.929 --> 21:05.022
We will eliminate them
as we retreat.

21:05.698 --> 21:06.255
Roger!

21:11.637 --> 21:14.572
We were saved!

21:15.274 --> 21:20.112
Imagine what would
have happened...

21:20.112 --> 21:22.481
...if we'd surrendered to them?

21:22.481 --> 21:24.917
But how did you know that they were ours?

21:24.917 --> 21:26.748
Those space-time bubble in front?

21:27.820 --> 21:29.811
I'd like to know that, too.

21:29.989 --> 21:33.693
I can't imagine you had
anything to go on.

21:33.693 --> 21:35.354
That's a...

21:36.128 --> 21:37.322
...a military secret!

21:38.664 --> 21:40.564
It was all intuition.

21:41.167 --> 21:43.002
How dare you be so rude.

21:43.002 --> 21:44.971
I just wasn't sure. That's all.

21:44.971 --> 21:48.341
We were about to
run out of anti-matter fuel.

21:48.341 --> 21:50.109
We really had our hands tied.

21:50.109 --> 21:53.169
And I had to make a decision
one way or another.

21:54.247 --> 21:57.016
But you seemed so confident
about it.

21:57.016 --> 22:01.453
It's more pathetic to see an unsure
captain than a dead captain.

22:02.455 --> 22:03.656
And...

22:03.656 --> 22:05.858
"When unsure,
you should always go forward."

22:05.858 --> 22:08.327
You told me that once.

22:08.327 --> 22:11.125
Is that all it was?

22:15.401 --> 22:17.460
What's so funny, Jinto?

22:17.770 --> 22:19.338
It's just that... well...

22:19.338 --> 22:22.933
I'll make sure we keep this
a secret from everybody.

22:23.276 --> 22:26.439
I think that's wise...

22:35.087 --> 22:38.824
So the main forces of the enemy
have moved on to Wimpel?

22:38.824 --> 22:40.121
Yes.

22:40.293 --> 22:43.353
The reconnaissance ships in the
Aptic region have confirmed it.

22:44.297 --> 22:45.998
In that case...

22:45.998 --> 22:50.196
...Aptic is going to be the main
target of the enemy assault.

22:54.240 --> 22:58.540
kizukanaikoto ga
The things I did not notice

22:59.078 --> 23:03.344
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

23:04.583 --> 23:08.280
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:09.522 --> 23:13.322
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:13.592 --> 23:15.561
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:15.561 --> 23:19.554
haritsumeta kimochiga
This tense feeling

23:20.766 --> 23:25.938
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keeping facing forward

23:25.938 --> 23:29.669
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:29.909 --> 23:34.073
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:34.613 --> 23:38.984
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:38.984 --> 23:46.192
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:46.192 --> 23:51.464
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:51.464 --> 24:00.031
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

24:02.007 --> 24:07.146
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:07.146 --> 24:12.551
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our joined hands and our finger tips

24:12.551 --> 24:20.925
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:21.360 --> 24:25.626
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:31.871 --> 24:34.073
You seriously think
she's calm?!

24:34.073 --> 24:36.909
More than I thought she would be.

24:36.909 --> 24:40.811
It seems to me that she feels
a little out of place here.

24:41.647 --> 24:45.310
Maybe she's not suited
to taking orders from above.

24:46.619 --> 24:47.381
A toast!

24:47.887 --> 24:50.089
They either need to give her
more power...

24:50.089 --> 24:53.320
...or maybe it would be better
if she acted alone.

24:53.592 --> 24:55.060
Out of place, huh?

24:55.060 --> 24:57.863
Come to think of it, that kid said
something along those lines.

24:57.863 --> 25:00.798
Next Episode...
The Eve of the Decisive Battle
